# WASM 2.11: Error Message Quality — WASM-Specific Error Codes, Stack Traces, and Recovery Guidance

## Problem
WASM errors are notoriously unhelpful: "RuntimeError: unreachable executed", "out of bounds memory access", "null function reference". Users need:
1. Human-readable error messages with context
2. Error codes they can search for
3. Recovery guidance ("try X to fix this")
4. Stack traces that map back to SQL context

## Implementation

### Error Type Hierarchy
```typescript
// In @frankensqlite/sdk
export class FrankenDBError extends Error {
  constructor(
    message: string,
    public readonly code: FrankenDBErrorCode,
    public readonly sql?: string,           // The SQL that caused it
    public readonly detail?: string,         // Internal detail
    public readonly recovery?: string,       // Suggested fix
  ) {
    super(`[${code}] ${message}`);
    this.name = 'FrankenDBError';
  }
}

export enum FrankenDBErrorCode {
  // Init errors (1xxx)
  WASM_LOAD_FAILED = 'FSQL1001',
  WORKER_INIT_FAILED = 'FSQL1002',
  OPFS_NOT_AVAILABLE = 'FSQL1003',
  SAB_NOT_AVAILABLE = 'FSQL1004',    // SharedArrayBuffer unavailable (missing COOP/COEP)
  MEMORY_LIMIT_EXCEEDED = 'FSQL1005',

  // SQL errors (2xxx)
  SQL_SYNTAX_ERROR = 'FSQL2001',
  CONSTRAINT_VIOLATION = 'FSQL2002',
  TABLE_NOT_FOUND = 'FSQL2003',
  TYPE_MISMATCH = 'FSQL2004',

  // Runtime errors (3xxx)
  DB_LOCKED = 'FSQL3001',            // SQLITE_BUSY equivalent
  WORKER_CRASHED = 'FSQL3002',
  OOM = 'FSQL3003',
  CORRUPTION_DETECTED = 'FSQL3004',

  // Persistence errors (4xxx)
  OPFS_WRITE_FAILED = 'FSQL4001',
  IDB_QUOTA_EXCEEDED = 'FSQL4002',
  EXPORT_FAILED = 'FSQL4003',
}
```

### Error Wrapping in Worker Bridge
```typescript
// In worker-bridge.ts
function wrapWasmError(raw: unknown, sql?: string): FrankenDBError {
  if (raw instanceof Error) {
    // Map WASM traps to user-friendly errors
    if (raw.message.includes('unreachable')) {
      return new FrankenDBError(
        'Internal WASM error — this is likely a bug in FrankenSQLite',
        FrankenDBErrorCode.WORKER_CRASHED,
        sql,
        raw.message,
        'Please report this at https://github.com/frankensqlite/issues with the SQL that triggered it'
      );
    }
    if (raw.message.includes('out of bounds')) {
      return new FrankenDBError(
        'WASM memory limit exceeded',
        FrankenDBErrorCode.OOM,
        sql,
        raw.message,
        'Try reducing the result set size (add LIMIT), or increase memory with FrankenDB.open({ memory: { maxPages: 65536 } })'
      );
    }
    // Parse SQLite error messages from Rust
    const sqliteMatch = raw.message.match(/sqlite error (\d+): (.+)/i);
    if (sqliteMatch) {
      return mapSqliteError(parseInt(sqliteMatch[1]), sqliteMatch[2], sql);
    }
  }
  return new FrankenDBError(
    String(raw),
    FrankenDBErrorCode.WORKER_CRASHED,
    sql,
    undefined,
    'Unexpected error — check browser console for details'
  );
}
```

### COOP/COEP Detection with Helpful Message
```typescript
// On SDK init: check for common misconfigurations
function checkEnvironment(): void {
  if (typeof SharedArrayBuffer === 'undefined') {
    console.warn(
      '[FrankenDB] SharedArrayBuffer is not available.\n' +
      'This usually means your server is missing COOP/COEP headers.\n' +
      'Add these headers to your server:\n' +
      '  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin\n' +
      '  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp\n' +
      'FrankenDB will fall back to single-writer mode.'
    );
  }

  if (typeof navigator?.storage?.getDirectory !== 'function') {
    console.warn(
      '[FrankenDB] OPFS is not available in this browser.\n' +
      'FrankenDB will fall back to IndexedDB for persistence.\n' +
      'For best performance, use Chrome 86+ or Firefox 111+.'
    );
  }
}
```

