# Task 2.6: JavaScript Value Conversion Layer

## What
Implement high-fidelity bidirectional conversion between SQLite values and JavaScript values.

## Type Mapping
| SQLite Type | JavaScript Type | Notes |
|-------------|-----------------|-------|
| NULL | null | |
| INTEGER | number/BigInt | Use BigInt for values > 2^53 |
| REAL | number | Standard IEEE 754 |
| TEXT | string | UTF-8 → UTF-16 automatic |
| BLOB | Uint8Array | Zero-copy when possible |

## Implementation
```rust
fn sqlite_to_js(val: &SqliteValue) -> JsValue {
    match val {
        SqliteValue::Null => JsValue::NULL,
        SqliteValue::Integer(i) => {
            if *i > (1i64 << 53) || *i < -(1i64 << 53) {
                js_sys::BigInt::from(*i).into()
            } else {
                JsValue::from_f64(*i as f64)
            }
        }
        SqliteValue::Float(f) => JsValue::from_f64(*f),
        SqliteValue::Text(s) => JsValue::from_str(s),
        SqliteValue::Blob(b) => {
            let arr = js_sys::Uint8Array::new_with_length(b.len() as u32);
            arr.copy_from(b);
            arr.into()
        }
    }
}

fn js_to_sqlite(val: JsValue) -> Result<SqliteValue, JsValue> {
    if val.is_null() || val.is_undefined() { return Ok(SqliteValue::Null); }
    if let Some(b) = val.as_bool() { return Ok(SqliteValue::Integer(if b { 1 } else { 0 })); }
    if let Some(f) = val.as_f64() {
        if f.fract() == 0.0 && f.abs() < (1i64 << 53) as f64 {
            return Ok(SqliteValue::Integer(f as i64));
        }
        return Ok(SqliteValue::Float(f));
    }
    if let Some(s) = val.as_string() { return Ok(SqliteValue::Text(s)); }
    if val.is_instance_of::<js_sys::Uint8Array>() {
        let arr = js_sys::Uint8Array::from(val);
        return Ok(SqliteValue::Blob(arr.to_vec()));
    }
    if val.is_instance_of::<js_sys::BigInt>() {
        // Parse BigInt to i64
        let s = js_sys::BigInt::from(val).to_string(10).unwrap().as_string().unwrap();
        let i: i64 = s.parse().map_err(|_| JsValue::from_str("BigInt too large for SQLite INTEGER"))?;
        return Ok(SqliteValue::Integer(i));
    }
    Err(JsValue::from_str("Unsupported JavaScript type for SQLite parameter"))
}
```

## Edge Cases
- NaN → NULL (SQLite has no NaN)
- Infinity → error (SQLite has no Infinity)
- Date objects → TEXT (ISO 8601 string) or INTEGER (Unix timestamp)
- undefined → NULL
- BigInt overflow (> i64::MAX) → error with helpful message

## Acceptance Criteria
- All SQLite types round-trip correctly through JS
- BigInt correctly handles values > Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER
- Blob uses Uint8Array efficiently
- Clear error messages for unsupported types

