        assert_eq!(count, 1, "uncommitted transaction must not be visible after crash");
        Ok::<_, FrankenError>(())
    });

    assert!(report.oracle_report.all_passed(), "oracle failures:\n{}", report.oracle_report);
}
```

### Additional FrankenSQLite Requirements (Bead-local)

These are *implementation-facing* requirements to make the test harness maximally useful.

1. Logging/tracing MUST include:
   - lab seed, worker_count, max_steps, and deterministic schedule trace hash
   - for each injected fault: fault kind, file glob, offset or sync index, and when it triggered
   - for cancellation injection: injection strategy, which await-point ID triggered, and task name
2. Test failures MUST print:
   - the last N scheduling decisions (task_id, poll_count, wake reason)
   - oracle failure summaries (not just "failed")
   - any invariants violated (and the minimal reproduction seed)
3. Every harness-level E2E test MUST support a `--replay <trace>` mode (or equivalent bead) so that a failure can be deterministically re-run.

