# Enable VDBE JOIN routing — currently disabled pending conformance

## Location
`crates/fsqlite-core/src/connection.rs:7935-7939`:
```rust
// TODO(perf): Enable VDBE JOIN routing when codegen_join_select
// passes all conformance tests:
// if has_joins(select) && !has_subquery_source(select) {
//     ... try compile_table_select -> execute_table_program ...
// }
```

Also at line 27737-27739:
```rust
/// Currently unused -- will be enabled when codegen_join_select passes conformance.
#[allow(dead_code)]
fn select_join_is_vdbe_eligible(select: &SelectStatement) -> bool {
```

## Impact
ALL JOIN queries take the slower connection-level fallback path instead of compiled VDBE bytecode. JOINs are extremely common in real-world SQL (nearly every non-trivial query has at least one JOIN), so this affects the majority of workload performance.

The codegen infrastructure exists (`codegen_join_select`) and the eligibility check function exists (`select_join_is_vdbe_eligible`). The blocker is conformance validation — some JOIN patterns produce incorrect results through the VDBE path.

## Required Fix
1. Run the full conformance suite through the VDBE JOIN path to identify failing cases
2. Fix the codegen bugs that produce incorrect results
3. Uncomment the routing code and remove the dead_code allow
4. Keep the fallback for unsupported patterns (e.g., subquery sources)

## Test Plan
- Enable VDBE JOIN routing for a subset of simple JOINs first (INNER JOIN on equality)
- Progressively expand to LEFT/RIGHT/CROSS/NATURAL
- All 1444+ conformance oracle tests must pass

