## B4.2 Next Slice: SimpleRowidRangeScan query_row (pane 3)

### Edit surface
`connection.rs:8503` — replace the remaining `SimpleRowidRangeScan` arm in the `Ok(None)` catch-all with a direct MemDB range scan.

### Implementation (~25 lines)
```rust
PreparedQueryFastPath::SimpleRowidRangeScan {
    root_page,
    lower_parameter_index,
    upper_parameter_index,
    rowid_alias_column_index,
} => {
    if !self.memdb_storage_count_shortcuts_safe.get() {
        return Ok(None);
    }
    let lower = params.and_then(|p| p.get(lower_parameter_index))
        .map(SqliteValue::to_integer).unwrap_or(i64::MIN);
    let upper = params.and_then(|p| p.get(upper_parameter_index))
        .map(SqliteValue::to_integer).unwrap_or(i64::MAX);
    let db = self.db.borrow();
    let table = db.get_table(root_page)?;
    let mut found_row = None;
    for (rowid, values) in table.iter_rows_in_rowid_range(lower, upper) {
        if found_row.is_some() {
            return Ok(Some(QueryRowCollectionOutcome::MultipleRows));
        }
        let mut row_vec = values.to_vec();
        if let Some(ipk_idx) = rowid_alias_column_index {
            if let Some(slot) = row_vec.get_mut(ipk_idx) {
                *slot = SqliteValue::Integer(rowid);
            }
        }
        found_row = Some(row_vec);
    }
    match found_row {
        Some(row) => Ok(Some(QueryRowCollectionOutcome::Row(Row { values: row }))),
        None => Ok(Some(QueryRowCollectionOutcome::NoRows)),
    }
}
```

### Why this is highest EV
- `iter_rows_in_rowid_range` uses binary search (O(log N) + O(range)) — much faster than VDBE engine startup
- Same pattern as B4.1, disjoint edit surface
- query_row is the hot path for mixed OLTP workloads (single-row lookups)

### Expected win
Eliminates VDBE engine creation + program execution for `SELECT * FROM t WHERE rowid BETWEEN ?1 AND ?2` with query_row. For the OLTP benchmark, this is ~10-50us saved per single-row range lookup.

